This product bundles no third-party source, but depends on the following
packages at runtime. Their licenses are permissive or weak-copyleft and are
compatible with this project's MIT license. Run `pip-licenses` for the full,
current list with versions.

Runtime dependencies and license families:
  - FastAPI, Starlette, Uvicorn, Pydantic ......... MIT
  - httpx, pdfplumber, pypdf, pytesseract ......... MIT / BSD
  - pypdfium2 .................................... Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause
    (PDF rendering; a permissive replacement for the AGPL-licensed PyMuPDF)
  - Pillow ....................................... MIT-CMU
  - arabic-reshaper .............................. MIT
  - python-bidi .................................. LGPL-3.0 (used unmodified)
  - python-docx .................................. MIT

Development-only tooling (not distributed with the service):
  - pytest, ruff, mypy, coverage ................. MIT / Apache-2.0
  - fpdf2 (synthetic test-PDF authoring) ......... LGPL-3.0 (used unmodified)

All sample, demo and test data in this repository is synthetic:

  - Person names are invented. Common first/last-name combinations may match
    real people by coincidence; no real person is described.
  - Employers and universities are fictional placeholders ("Demo Organization",
    "Example Company", "Demo University", ...). No real organisation is named.
  - E-mail addresses use the RFC 2606 reserved domains (example.com, example.org,
    example.net, and the .test TLD), which reach no inbox; the extractor treats
    them as placeholders by design. The few parser, de-duplication and
    multi-CV tests that need an address the extractor accepts as real use
    contoso.com and fabrikam.com, Microsoft's documentation domains for
    fictional companies.
  - Phone numbers come from the North American 555-0100 to 555-0199 range,
    which is reserved for fictional use.
  - Real city names (e.g. Riyadh, Jeddah, Dammam) appear only as location lines,
    for realism.
